-- title:
--   Finiteness of Čech H¹ for chart-finite two-chart data
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and let $\mathcal U$ be a two-chart cover over $R$, that is, $R$-algebras $A_0$, $A_1$, $A_{01}$ together with $R$-algebra maps $\rho_0 : A_0 \to A_{01}$ and $\rho_1 : A_1 \to A_{01}$. Let $S$ be a sections datum for $\mathcal U$: modules $M_0$ over $A_0$, $M_1$ over $A_1$ and $M_{01}$ over $A_{01}$, each also an $R$-module with the scalar actions forming towers over $R$, together with $R$-linear maps $r_0 : M_0 \to M_{01}$ and $r_1 : M_1 \to M_{01}$ satisfying $r_0(a \cdot m) = \rho_0(a) \cdot r_0(m)$ for $a \in A_0$ and $r_1(a \cdot m) = \rho_1(a) \cdot r_1(m)$ for $a \in A_1$. Assume given $f \in A_0$ and $g \in A_1$ with $\rho_0(f)\,\rho_1(g) = 1$ in $A_{01}$; that $M_0$ is a finite module over the $R$-subalgebra of $A_0$ generated by $f$, namely `Algebra.adjoin R {f}`; that for every $m \in M_{01}$ there is $n \in \mathbb N$ with $\rho_0(f)^n \cdot m$ in the image of $r_0$; and that for every $m \in M_{01}$ there is $n \in \mathbb N$ with $\rho_1(g)^n \cdot m$ in the image of $r_1$. Then `S.H1`, the quotient of $M_{01}$ by the image of the Čech differential $(x,y) \mapsto r_1(y) - r_0(x)$ on $M_0 \times M_1$, i.e. by $r_0(M_0) + r_1(M_1)$, is a finitely generated $R$-module.
--
--   This is Serre's computation of $H^1$ on the projective line in elementary two-chart form: finiteness of the first Čech cohomology of a sections datum whose chart $M_0$ is finite over the polynomial subalgebra $R[f]$, with no Noetherian hypothesis on $R$. It is the $H^1$ half of the finiteness theorem for the Čech cohomology of a proper curve admitting a finite map to $\mathbb P^1_R$, and is used by [`TwoChartCech.Sections.finite_H0_of_chartFinite`](thm.html#TwoChartCech.Sections.finite_H0_of_chartFinite) and by the finiteness statements for line bundles and sections data on smooth proper curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_TwoChartCech_Sections_finite_H1_of_chartFinite.lean

import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicGeometry_TwoChartCech
